Lesson 22: Enums aur Literal Types in TypeScript 🚀
Aaj hum seekhenge ki jab kisi variable mein sirf kuch fixed values allowed hon, toh unhe TypeScript mein kaise define karte hain.
1. Literal Types
Maan lo order ka status sirf "pending", "shipped" ya "delivered" ho sakta hai.
let status: "pending" | "shipped" | "delivered";

status = "pending";   // ✅
status = "delivered"; // ✅

// status = "cancelled"; // ❌ Error


Yahan status mein sirf ye teen values allowed hain.
Isse union of string literal types kehte hain.
Real-world example
type UserRole = "admin" | "user" | "manager";

function login(role: UserRole) {
  console.log("Logged in as " + role);
}

login("admin"); // ✅
login("user");  // ✅
// login("guest"); // ❌ Error


Kab use karein? Jab fixed strings ki chhoti list ho, jaise status, roles, themes ya payment methods.

2. Enums
enum bhi related fixed values ko group karne ka tareeka hai.
enum OrderStatus {
  Pending,
  Shipped,
  Delivered
}

let status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.Pending;

console.log(status); // 0


By default, numeric enums 0 se start hote hain:
Enum member	Value
Pending	0
Shipped	1
Delivered	2
Agar string values chahiye:
enum OrderStatus {
  Pending = "PENDING",
  Shipped = "SHIPPED",
  Delivered = "DELIVERED"
}

let status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.Pending;

console.log(status); // PENDING


3. Literal Types vs Enums
Literal types	Enums
"pending" \| "shipped"	OrderStatus.Pending
Simple fixed values ke liye	Named group of constants ke liye
Runtime par alag enum object nahi banta	Normal enums runtime JavaScript code generate karte hain
Modern TypeScript mein fixed string values ke liye literal unions kaafi useful hain. Enums bhi valid option hain, especially jab named enum members chahiye hon.
